<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nara is a city in the Kansai region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the capital of Nara Prefecture. The surrounding Nara basin was the heartland of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamato-court">Yamato kingship</a>, and from 710 to 784 the planned capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heijo-kyo">Heijō-kyō</a> on the site gave its name to the Nara period. Its great temples, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/todai-ji">Tōdai-ji</a> with its giant bronze Buddha, are a World Heritage Site.</p></div>
